From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: ov08d10: validate exposure timing reads

SMBus byte reads return a signed error or a byte. Preserve read errors
instead of truncating them into timing bytes and programming exposure
from invalid data. Reject a zero combined HTS before division.

The original Intel/Linux attribution is retained. Valid register tables,
exposure conversion, VTS policy and board configuration are unchanged.
This does not qualify physical exposure, VBLANK coupling or calibration.
Signed-off-by: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov08d10.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov08d10.c
@@ -784,9 +784,17 @@ static int ov08d10_set_exposure(struct ov08d10 *ov08d10, u32 exposure)
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
-	hts_h = i2c_smbus_read_byte_data(client, 0x37);
-	hts_l = i2c_smbus_read_byte_data(client, 0x38);
+	ret = i2c_smbus_read_byte_data(client, 0x37);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+	hts_h = ret;
+	ret = i2c_smbus_read_byte_data(client, 0x38);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+	hts_l = ret;
 	hts = ((hts_h << 8) | (hts_l));
+	if (!hts)
+		return -EINVAL;
 	exp_cal = 66 * OV08D10_ROWCLK / hts;
 	exposure = exposure * exp_cal / (cur_vts - OV08D10_EXPOSURE_MAX_MARGIN);
 	/* CIS control registers */
